Renge is the entity [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] Marchal serve. Anaïs calls her his lady, and the Fickle Mistress. Where [[Aut]] designs the path a story should take, Renge is everything that might happen along the way: chance, and the room to choose. She and Aut are at odds for it.

She gives her followers little direction. Anaïs has not spoken with her in years; she leaves the occasional message, and he has had no conversation with her since long before he joined [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. She may grant a great boon or land a terrible bane, and that uncertainty keeps her short of friends.

Renge counts any being too powerful to be overcome a balance breaker, and anything too insurmountable makes for a poor story. She helped slay [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]], a god that once threatened the world, and she tried and failed to stop the assassination of the previous prime minister. She is found in the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]]. The Pontifex is no friend of hers, and the leaders of the great Orgs are not friends of the narrative siblings.
